ioshock with  players able to mix and match weapons  and powers like electricity and  telekinesis to rip through anything that  stands in their way the game is also  scored by Mick Gordon The Man Behind the  face meltingly great Doom 2016  soundtrack rise of the Ronin is a brand  new action game from Team ninja the  studio behind Neo and Ninja Gaiden it's  an open world RPG set in the late 19th  century in Japan and if previous team  ninja games are anything to go by combat  will be incredibly important and  probably very difficult it's set to  launch in 2024 and will be a PlayStation  console exclusive at the 2022 game  awards hideo Kojima took to the stage to  reveal a sequel to 2019's hit death  stranding with death stranding Kojima  and his team created a new genre aiming  at Connecting People which was oddly  prescient given the impact of the  pandemic which happened a few months  later the sequel is set to bring back a  lot of faces from the original game  including Leia saidu's fragile and  Norman Reedus as Sam Porter Bridges  Contraband is an upcoming Co-op  Smuggler's Paradise from Avalanche  Studios the team behind the just cause  series we don't know much about the game  just yet other than it's set in the  1970s in the fictual world of Bayan and  it's an Xbox console exclusive Dragon's  Dogma was a cult hit when it was  released in 2012. it was a fun take on a  traditional open world fantasy RPG and  gave the player pawns which are AI  controlled party members that could be  shared online with other players a  sequel is being developed using capcom's  re engine which the company is using for  the Resident Evil remix and used on  Devil May Cry 5. it's hard to believe  it's almost been 10 years since the  launch of Dragon Age Inquisition but  we're finally finally getting a sequel  in Dragon Age dread wolf one that sets  to put everyone's beloved egg Mage Solas  firmly into the role of antagonist  there's no release date for dread wolf  just yet but the game recently completed  its Alpha Milestone and is completely  playable from beginning to end  Inquisition wasn't strictly an open  world game and there's no guarantee that  dread wolf will be one but if the amount  of time I spent in the Hinterlands  counts for anything then it is an  honorary open world game a new Fable was  confirmed to be in development back in  2020 but since then we've barely heard  anything about it the Beloved uniquely  British franchise has been dormant at  Xbox for a number of years but now it's  being rebooted by playground games who  you may know as the team responsible for  Forza Horizon so there you have it 25  upcoming open world games that are set  to launch in 2023 and Beyond to keep up  to date on all of them make sure to  subscribe to Gamespot on YouTube or  check out gamespot.com I'm on Twitter at  Lucy James games and I'll see you next  time
 

